# NOTICE

dsh-desktop is an independent macOS desktop shell for the official
[DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)
(`@deepseek-ai/dsh`). The Harness itself, including its Web UI and plugin
runtime, is authored by DeepSeek and licensed under the MIT License.

## Architecture attribution

The desktop shell architecture — Electron main process supervising a
loopback `dsh web` child on an OS-assigned port, parsing the canonical
`dsh web: http://127.0.0.1:<port>` readiness line, tray-owned host lifecycle,
`ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE` reuse of the bundled Node runtime, and staging a
self-contained host dependency closure for packaging — is adapted from:

- [anywhere-labs/deepseek-harness-desktop](https://github.com/anywhere-labs/deepseek-harness-desktop)
  (MIT License) — `apps/desktop`: host-supervisor, window-lifecycle, staging
  and packaging patterns.
- [dawangcoding/ClawUI](https://github.com/dawangcoding/ClawUI) — child-process
  gateway state machine and diagnostics-logging patterns.

Third-party packages retain their own licenses.
